text:
Whoever is fortunate will be loved;

        and I in love do not wish to be fortunate,

        since, envious of my own evil,

        I count it fortune to be so unfortunate for you.


        Only this is service: to serve without being rewarded;

        the lucky man is close to coarse;

        to follow good is compulsory for all,

        I alone follow evil without being forced.


        I have no need of fortune to love you;

        I love in you what I understand of you,

        not what I hope for, because I hope for nothing;


        knowing you carries me to adore you;

        to serve, but only for serving, is what I seek;

        from you I want no more than what I love in you.
